1
00:00:06,004 --> 00:00:07,594
Bye-bye, Kobato!

2
00:00:08,534 --> 00:00:10,834
Okay, see you on Monday!

3
00:00:14,314 --> 00:00:15,864
I'm sorry!

4
00:00:16,374 --> 00:00:18,144
What is it with you, always?

5
00:00:18,144 --> 00:00:19,484
Are you all right?

6
00:00:19,484 --> 00:00:20,684
Never mind, just get out of my way.

7
00:00:20,684 --> 00:00:21,654
I'm going to be late.

8
00:00:21,654 --> 00:00:23,384
Are you working tonight, too?

9
00:00:24,124 --> 00:00:25,174
Well yeah.

10
00:00:39,904 --> 00:00:41,304
Oh, Kobato.

11
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:42,404
Thanks for your help.

12
00:00:42,404 --> 00:00:44,774
Um, is there anything I can help you with?

13
00:00:45,074 --> 00:00:47,664
No, I'm fine. You can go home now.

14
00:00:56,054 --> 00:00:58,214
Part-time work
Job information

15
00:01:06,594 --> 00:01:09,734
Kobato.

16
00:01:09,734 --> 00:01:12,564
Kobato.
What should I do?

17
00:01:12,564 --> 00:01:16,974
Kobato.
Even the most obvious of things

18
00:01:17,874 --> 00:01:21,174
Are always such a challenge

19
00:01:21,174 --> 00:01:23,944
I want to laugh when I'm happy

20
00:01:23,944 --> 00:01:28,244
And sing whenever I want

21
00:01:28,814 --> 00:01:31,254
Is all

22
00:01:32,554 --> 00:01:36,924
They say my dreams will come true someday

23
00:01:37,364 --> 00:01:40,634
But when will "someday" come?

24
00:01:40,634 --> 00:01:44,124
I can't wait forever

25
00:01:44,264 --> 00:01:50,044
On "1, 2, 3!" I'll spread open my arms

26
00:01:50,044 --> 00:01:55,244
And let the light gather around me

27
00:01:55,244 --> 00:01:58,084
Where is it?

28
00:01:58,084 --> 00:02:01,414
Please tell me what I can do

29
00:02:01,414 --> 00:02:04,254
I make the most of getting hurt

30
00:02:04,254 --> 00:02:07,154
And run with all my might

31
00:02:07,154 --> 00:02:11,124
Despite how many dozens of times I fall

32
00:02:11,124 --> 00:02:14,164
And start crying

33
00:02:14,164 --> 00:02:18,194
I surprise myself

34
00:02:18,664 --> 00:02:22,834
In how much I believe in tomorrow

35
00:02:32,544 --> 00:02:34,784
...Detective Kobato Hanato.

36
00:02:34,784 --> 00:02:36,454
...Detective Kobato Hanato.
Wow...

37
00:02:36,954 --> 00:02:40,514
I didn't realize there were so
many different kinds of jobs.

38
00:02:40,624 --> 00:02:43,854
What do you plan to do with that book? Ouch!

39
00:02:44,124 --> 00:02:46,164
What else? I'm going to find a job!

40
00:02:46,164 --> 00:02:47,654
Just like Fujimoto!

41
00:02:48,064 --> 00:02:50,894
You want to help in any little way to
pay back that debt. Is that is?

42
00:02:51,034 --> 00:02:52,054
Yes!

43
00:02:55,474 --> 00:02:58,634
Like deliver newspapers in the fresh morning air.

44
00:02:58,774 --> 00:03:00,934
You always oversleep in the morning.

45
00:03:03,984 --> 00:03:05,774
Ah, well then...

46
00:03:07,314 --> 00:03:10,254
How about delivering
pizzas to everyone's homes?

47
00:03:10,254 --> 00:03:12,314
You will get lost and that's for certain.

48
00:03:16,694 --> 00:03:18,354
W-Well then...

49
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:21,794
Maybe I could help people move.

50
00:03:21,794 --> 00:03:24,024
I can just see you breaking an expensive vase.

51
00:03:26,874 --> 00:03:30,444
What?! Then what kind of job should I look for?

52
00:03:30,444 --> 00:03:31,704
Don't ask me!

53
00:03:33,874 --> 00:03:35,574
I give up!

54
00:03:36,344 --> 00:03:37,834
Ioryogi-san!

55
00:03:39,714 --> 00:03:41,254
Good evening!

56
00:03:41,254 --> 00:03:42,584
Yes?

57
00:03:44,254 --> 00:03:45,424
Oh no...

58
00:03:45,424 --> 00:03:46,974
It's got torn.

59
00:03:47,354 --> 00:03:48,794
The poor thing.

60
00:03:48,954 --> 00:03:49,994
Sorry.

61
00:03:49,994 --> 00:03:51,294
That's all right.

62
00:03:52,894 --> 00:03:54,394
There. All done.

63
00:03:54,394 --> 00:03:56,164
Thank you very much!

64
00:03:56,164 --> 00:03:57,364
No problem.

65
00:03:57,364 --> 00:04:00,564
Oh! There's one other favor I wanted to ask.

66
00:04:04,774 --> 00:04:06,574
Oh! The umbrella man!

67
00:04:06,644 --> 00:04:08,874
Oh yes, from the other day.

68
00:04:09,074 --> 00:04:11,384
Thank you for your kindness that day.

69
00:04:11,384 --> 00:04:12,014
Don't mention it.

70
00:04:12,014 --> 00:04:14,344
Oh? So I see you already know each other.

71
00:04:14,614 --> 00:04:17,084
Yes. Let me introduce myself properly.

72
00:04:17,084 --> 00:04:18,424
I'm Ueda, the manager of this shop.

73
00:04:18,424 --> 00:04:19,824
I'm Kobato Hanato!

74
00:04:20,084 --> 00:04:23,254
Kobato lives in our building.

75
00:04:23,454 --> 00:04:26,364
Her regular job is helping out
at Yomogi Kindergarten.

76
00:04:27,234 --> 00:04:31,534
She said she was looking for a
part-time job, so I thought of this shop.

77
00:04:31,864 --> 00:04:32,994
Is that right?

78
00:04:33,504 --> 00:04:38,034
Well we could certainly use your help,
in particular during the busy weekends.

79
00:04:38,204 --> 00:04:40,004
At least until my hands get better.

80
00:04:41,414 --> 00:04:42,964
Look at the shape they're in.

81
00:04:43,884 --> 00:04:45,614
What happened?

82
00:04:45,614 --> 00:04:48,744
Well... I can be clumsy sometimes and...

83
00:04:49,184 --> 00:04:52,244
She apparently injured herself the other day.

84
00:04:52,454 --> 00:04:54,114
Are you okay?

85
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:58,154
Mhm. It's just that the manager has to also
cover for me when it gets busy.

86
00:04:59,024 --> 00:05:01,124
Kobato, you would be a great help.

87
00:05:01,434 --> 00:05:04,424
Yes, Mr. Manager, I would very
much like to help out.

88
00:05:04,964 --> 00:05:07,064
And you... uh...

89
00:05:07,134 --> 00:05:10,904
I'm Yumi Omura. Welcome aboard, Kobato.

90
00:05:13,344 --> 00:05:15,644
I hope you enjoy your job, Kobato.

91
00:05:15,644 --> 00:05:16,804
Yes!

92
00:05:21,454 --> 00:05:22,914
I'm changed!

93
00:05:26,124 --> 00:05:28,884
Oh good. The uniform fits you perfectly.

94
00:05:29,224 --> 00:05:31,924
So, what would you like me to do?

95
00:05:32,964 --> 00:05:37,554
Um... Well, you could begin by
cheerfully welcoming customers?

96
00:05:37,664 --> 00:05:39,434
Hi! Good afternoon!

97
00:05:39,434 --> 00:05:41,074
Ah, y-yes, something like that.

98
00:05:41,074 --> 00:05:41,934
Yes!

99
00:05:41,934 --> 00:05:46,734
Then after you take their order
put the cakes in those boxes.

100
00:05:46,974 --> 00:05:48,104
These here?

101
00:05:48,374 --> 00:05:51,514
I'll handle the cash register.
You take their money.

102
00:05:51,514 --> 00:05:54,084
And "Thank you very much!" Right?

103
00:05:54,084 --> 00:05:55,344
That's right!

104
00:05:56,914 --> 00:05:58,184
Hello.

105
00:05:58,184 --> 00:05:59,684
Hello!

106
00:05:59,684 --> 00:06:01,924
Well then, shall we give it a try?

107
00:06:01,924 --> 00:06:03,014
Yes!

108
00:06:03,354 --> 00:06:09,494
Umm... I'll have the strawberry shortcake...
the Mont Blanc cake... and um...

109
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:10,564
Strawberry shortcake, Mont Blanc, cheese...
Umm... I'll have the strawberry shortcake...
the Mont Blanc cake... and um...

110
00:06:10,564 --> 00:06:13,674
Strawberry shortcake, Mont Blanc, cheese...
the cheesecake... no not that, the apple pie.
Oh and that lemon tart.

111
00:06:13,674 --> 00:06:15,104
apple... lemon... uhh...
the cheesecake... no not that, the apple pie.
Oh and that lemon tart.

112
00:06:15,104 --> 00:06:17,264
apple... lemon... uhh...

113
00:06:17,374 --> 00:06:20,034
Yes and one of those cream puffs, please.

114
00:06:20,344 --> 00:06:22,174
Uh... um...

115
00:06:22,174 --> 00:06:27,054
Strawberry shortcake, Mont Blanc, apple pie,
a lemon tart and a cream puff.

116
00:06:27,054 --> 00:06:28,884
What a memory! I'm impressed.

117
00:06:28,884 --> 00:06:30,654
Would you put them in a box Kobato?

118
00:06:30,654 --> 00:06:31,844
Ah, yes.

119
00:06:32,054 --> 00:06:34,684
Um... strawberry shortcake...

120
00:06:35,724 --> 00:06:36,854
I'm so sorry!

121
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:39,414
Relax. Will you get another one?

122
00:06:39,624 --> 00:06:41,024
Y-Yes.

123
00:06:44,604 --> 00:06:46,534
Kobato are you okay?

124
00:06:46,534 --> 00:06:48,164
Y-Yes!

125
00:06:51,574 --> 00:06:53,674
And also the Mont Blanc and...

126
00:06:53,674 --> 00:06:57,044
Apple pie, lemon tart and cream puff.

127
00:07:02,454 --> 00:07:04,314
It's ready!

128
00:07:05,724 --> 00:07:07,554
Then finally...

129
00:07:10,424 --> 00:07:12,024
Thank you very much!

130
00:07:12,024 --> 00:07:14,124
Thank you, cheerful shop assistant.

131
00:07:17,604 --> 00:07:19,034
Was that okay?

132
00:07:19,034 --> 00:07:21,734
Yes. I'm sure you'll be all right once
you get the hang of things.

133
00:07:22,404 --> 00:07:23,804
Hello!

134
00:07:23,804 --> 00:07:24,704
Huh?

135
00:07:24,704 --> 00:07:26,174
Kobato!

136
00:07:26,474 --> 00:07:28,344
Marina and Marina's mother!

137
00:07:28,344 --> 00:07:29,514
Hello!

138
00:07:29,514 --> 00:07:30,714
Hello.

139
00:07:30,714 --> 00:07:33,114
Kobato is a cake shop worker!

140
00:07:33,184 --> 00:07:35,654
Yes. Today I'm a cake shop worker.

141
00:07:35,654 --> 00:07:36,884
I'm jealous.

142
00:07:36,884 --> 00:07:38,584
Which cake would you like?

143
00:07:38,724 --> 00:07:41,984
We came to pick up my birthday cake today!

144
00:07:42,194 --> 00:07:46,124
Wow, it's your birthday?! Happy Birthday!

145
00:07:46,224 --> 00:07:48,254
Kobato, can you wrap it up for them?

146
00:07:48,364 --> 00:07:49,554
Yes!

147
00:07:53,164 --> 00:07:54,034
Here you go.

148
00:07:54,034 --> 00:07:55,024
Yes!

149
00:07:58,744 --> 00:08:00,904
Here you are. Sorry to keep you waiting.

150
00:08:01,314 --> 00:08:03,304
Thank you, Kobato.

151
00:08:04,084 --> 00:08:05,944
Thank you very much!

152
00:08:05,944 --> 00:08:07,544
See you!

153
00:08:15,324 --> 00:08:16,024
What's the matter?

154
00:08:16,024 --> 00:08:16,394
Happy Birthday Marina
What's the matter?

155
00:08:16,394 --> 00:08:17,164
Happy Birthday Marina

156
00:08:17,164 --> 00:08:19,394
Happy Birthday Marina
Why is this here?

157
00:08:19,394 --> 00:08:19,724
Happy Birthday Marina

158
00:08:19,994 --> 00:08:22,024
You may have put the wrong cake in the box!

159
00:08:22,764 --> 00:08:24,964
I'll try and catch Marina!

160
00:08:25,264 --> 00:08:26,994
Marina!

161
00:08:29,974 --> 00:08:31,874
Kobato, are you okay?

162
00:08:32,204 --> 00:08:33,764
Y-Yes...

163
00:08:34,344 --> 00:08:34,544
Bakery Tirol

164
00:08:34,544 --> 00:08:36,074
Bakery Tirol
Hello!

165
00:08:36,074 --> 00:08:37,444
Bakery Tirol
I'll have that and this one over here.

166
00:08:37,444 --> 00:08:38,344
Bakery Tirol
Right!

167
00:08:38,344 --> 00:08:42,054
Bakery Tirol
Kobato, that customer's asking for
Mont Blanc and cheesecake.

168
00:08:42,054 --> 00:08:43,924
Bakery Tirol
Oh no! I'm sorry!

169
00:08:43,924 --> 00:08:45,314
Bakery Tirol

170
00:08:48,954 --> 00:08:50,394
I'm all tired out.

171
00:08:50,394 --> 00:08:52,724
Good job, Kobato.

172
00:08:52,864 --> 00:08:54,984
Oh, thank you for your help!

173
00:08:55,564 --> 00:08:57,434
Here's something for you.

174
00:08:57,434 --> 00:08:59,764
Huh? Wow, thank you!

175
00:08:59,764 --> 00:09:01,734
Ioryogi-san will be pleased!

176
00:09:01,734 --> 00:09:02,804
Io?

177
00:09:02,804 --> 00:09:04,894
He's a stuffed doll in front of people.

178
00:09:06,044 --> 00:09:08,514
I'll be looking forward to your help tomorrow.

179
00:09:08,714 --> 00:09:11,114
Are you sure? You don't mind if I come again?

180
00:09:11,114 --> 00:09:13,144
Why, of course not.

181
00:09:13,144 --> 00:09:15,584
Yumi, thanks. You can go too.

182
00:09:15,584 --> 00:09:18,484
Oh but there's still cleanup to do.

183
00:09:18,484 --> 00:09:23,324
I'll take care of that. Your hands aren't
healed yet. Don't push yourself.

184
00:09:25,364 --> 00:09:26,584
Okay...

185
00:09:29,164 --> 00:09:31,324
Well then, Mr. Ueda. Good nigh...

186
00:09:37,074 --> 00:09:38,804
Good night, sir!

187
00:09:39,804 --> 00:09:42,534
Oh yes. Have a good night.

188
00:09:47,284 --> 00:09:49,084
Is something the matter?

189
00:09:50,054 --> 00:09:53,054
No. It's nothing.

190
00:09:53,054 --> 00:09:56,144
But Yumi, you seem to be
worried about something.

191
00:09:57,624 --> 00:10:00,064
I was just thinking about Mr. Ueda.

192
00:10:00,194 --> 00:10:01,894
Mr. Ueda?

193
00:10:01,894 --> 00:10:04,234
There seems to be something on his mind.

194
00:10:06,204 --> 00:10:10,104
I asked him about it once, but he
just said, "It's nothing."

195
00:10:10,434 --> 00:10:12,074
Oh is that right?

196
00:10:12,074 --> 00:10:13,804
The shop is doing well.

197
00:10:14,274 --> 00:10:17,974
Then what could it be that's bothering him?

198
00:10:19,444 --> 00:10:20,914
I wonder if he's in debt.

199
00:10:20,914 --> 00:10:21,754
What?

200
00:10:21,754 --> 00:10:24,724
Yomogi Kindergarten is in
trouble because of that.

201
00:10:24,724 --> 00:10:28,954
Kobato, is that why you decided
to start working with us?

202
00:10:28,954 --> 00:10:29,854
Yes!

203
00:10:29,854 --> 00:10:31,294
That is admirable.

204
00:10:31,294 --> 00:10:37,094
Oh no. What I'm doing is nothing
compared with Ms. Sayaka and Fujimoto.

205
00:10:37,364 --> 00:10:40,134
I just wanted to help in any way that I can.

206
00:10:42,734 --> 00:10:46,674
I wish I could help Mr. Ueda.

207
00:10:51,084 --> 00:10:52,604
Now this is incredibly delicious.

208
00:10:54,384 --> 00:10:58,214
It's tough not being able to help
out when you want to, isn't it?

209
00:10:59,454 --> 00:11:02,324
I'm going to find out what's bothering Mr. Ueda.

210
00:11:02,324 --> 00:11:06,694
Well, fine, but don't stick your nose
in too far and get yourself fired.

211
00:11:06,694 --> 00:11:08,964
I won't be able to have any more
of this delicious cake.

212
00:11:09,194 --> 00:11:12,794
Oh, but it might be good to work
at different kinds of places.

213
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:15,694
Sushi!

214
00:11:16,604 --> 00:11:17,974
How about a steakhouse?!

215
00:11:19,044 --> 00:11:20,664
Or classy Chinese cuisine?!

216
00:11:21,114 --> 00:11:24,234
So Kobato, where do you plan to work next?

217
00:11:24,314 --> 00:11:26,944
I plan to stay at the cake shop for awhile!

218
00:11:32,224 --> 00:11:33,854
Good morning!

219
00:11:33,854 --> 00:11:35,444
Good morning, Kobato.

220
00:11:35,754 --> 00:11:37,054
Good morning.

221
00:11:37,624 --> 00:11:39,964
Will you please line these cookies on the shelf?

222
00:11:39,964 --> 00:11:41,124
Yes, sir!

223
00:11:48,004 --> 00:11:49,974
Oh, please take care of things out here.

224
00:11:51,374 --> 00:11:54,844
Did he just sigh, looking at me?

225
00:11:54,844 --> 00:11:56,474
Huh? Did he do that?

226
00:11:57,074 --> 00:11:58,304
I wonder why.

227
00:11:58,984 --> 00:12:03,284
Could I have something to do with his problems?

228
00:12:20,934 --> 00:12:23,804
I'm going to ask Mr. Ueda what the problem is.

229
00:12:25,044 --> 00:12:26,344
Trust me!

230
00:12:26,344 --> 00:12:30,034
Are you sure? Then... ask
him nonchalantly, okay?

231
00:12:30,844 --> 00:12:32,974
Okay! Kobato is ready!

232
00:12:48,894 --> 00:12:50,124
Excuse me...

233
00:12:50,664 --> 00:12:51,764
Kobato?

234
00:12:51,764 --> 00:12:53,994
Yes. Um, actually I...

235
00:12:54,634 --> 00:12:57,534
There's something I want
to nonchalantly ask you!

236
00:12:57,674 --> 00:12:58,934
Kobato?!

237
00:13:00,914 --> 00:13:01,874
What is it?

238
00:13:02,174 --> 00:13:06,114
I'm wondering. Is there perhaps
something that is worrying you?

239
00:13:08,384 --> 00:13:10,954
Everything is fine. Nothing's worrying me.

240
00:13:10,954 --> 00:13:12,054
But...

241
00:13:12,054 --> 00:13:14,224
Yumi told me that you were
deep in thought sometimes,

242
00:13:14,224 --> 00:13:18,454
or that you seemed like you
wanted to say something.

243
00:13:18,694 --> 00:13:20,094
That something's wrong.

244
00:13:21,834 --> 00:13:24,524
It's nothing that Yumi should
be concerning herself with.

245
00:13:25,664 --> 00:13:26,804
That's what he says.

246
00:13:26,804 --> 00:13:29,774
That makes me more curious than ever.

247
00:13:31,704 --> 00:13:33,004
Good morning.

248
00:13:33,004 --> 00:13:33,874
Oh?

249
00:13:33,874 --> 00:13:34,974
Kobato?

250
00:13:34,974 --> 00:13:36,544
Ms. Sayaka!

251
00:13:36,544 --> 00:13:37,914
What are you doing here?

252
00:13:37,914 --> 00:13:41,314
She's helping us out until my hands get better.

253
00:13:41,314 --> 00:13:42,684
Oh is that right?

254
00:13:43,014 --> 00:13:44,344
Would you like some cake?

255
00:13:44,654 --> 00:13:49,094
I'm heading over to Chitose's place for a visit
and I thought I'd pick something up for her.

256
00:13:50,024 --> 00:13:52,684
It's been a while since I bought
something from Bakery Tirol.

257
00:13:53,124 --> 00:13:58,394
You once ordered a birthday cake
for your husband, didn't you?

258
00:13:59,034 --> 00:14:00,864
Uh... yes...

259
00:14:07,474 --> 00:14:10,004
Ms. Sayaka's husband?

260
00:14:10,674 --> 00:14:13,074
I guess that means that she's
married and has a husband.

261
00:14:13,184 --> 00:14:15,814
But I've never met him.

262
00:14:16,114 --> 00:14:17,984
Maybe they split up then.

263
00:14:21,954 --> 00:14:25,254
Ms. Sayaka seemed lonely.

264
00:14:26,364 --> 00:14:28,954
Don't ask her about this openly.

265
00:14:29,434 --> 00:14:30,764
Why shouldn't I?

266
00:14:30,764 --> 00:14:33,164
There are some things people
don't want to talk about.

267
00:14:33,964 --> 00:14:37,964
You're keeping quiet about working to
help the kindergarten, aren't you?

268
00:14:38,474 --> 00:14:41,404
Everyone has their own secrets.

269
00:14:44,344 --> 00:14:47,074
Do you think that the Bakery Tirol manager
is keeping something secret too?

270
00:14:48,214 --> 00:14:53,784
But Yumi really wants to know. So in
that case, what should be done?

271
00:14:53,884 --> 00:14:56,654
Investigate secretly, I guess.

272
00:14:57,594 --> 00:15:00,184
A job that I doubt is suited for a Dobato, though.

273
00:15:01,194 --> 00:15:02,854
But I'll do my best!

274
00:15:06,764 --> 00:15:08,494
Thank you very much!

275
00:15:12,044 --> 00:15:14,714
Being secretive... I guess...

276
00:15:14,714 --> 00:15:16,474
Hey, it's Kobato!

277
00:15:17,174 --> 00:15:18,474
What are you doing?

278
00:15:18,714 --> 00:15:20,304
I'm secretly investigating.

279
00:15:20,444 --> 00:15:21,714
Wow, cool!

280
00:15:21,714 --> 00:15:23,304
Like a detective!

281
00:15:24,114 --> 00:15:25,584
A detective?

282
00:15:26,824 --> 00:15:28,684
Wow...

283
00:15:28,824 --> 00:15:30,794
So this is what a detective does.

284
00:15:30,964 --> 00:15:31,524
Yeah.

285
00:15:31,524 --> 00:15:32,424
That's right.
Yeah.

286
00:15:32,964 --> 00:15:38,104
A detective investigates a lot, like
motive and alibi, proof and so on,

287
00:15:38,104 --> 00:15:41,724
asks a lot of questions and follows
people and stuff like that, right?

288
00:15:41,934 --> 00:15:42,974
Cool!

289
00:15:42,974 --> 00:15:44,804
We'll help!

290
00:15:45,944 --> 00:15:48,874
No. A detective works alone!

291
00:15:49,174 --> 00:15:50,704
Oh, I see.

292
00:15:51,244 --> 00:15:53,774
You're going way off tangent here!

293
00:15:55,414 --> 00:15:57,314
Thank you very much!

294
00:16:00,384 --> 00:16:02,114
Um, excuse me!

295
00:16:02,754 --> 00:16:05,754
Um, today, I'm a detective!

296
00:16:05,994 --> 00:16:07,924
What? A detective?

297
00:16:08,294 --> 00:16:10,734
Did you notice anything unusual at Bakery Tirol?

298
00:16:10,904 --> 00:16:12,234
No, not really.

299
00:16:12,234 --> 00:16:14,404
Uh, are you working on a case?

300
00:16:14,404 --> 00:16:17,774
Yes. It's the case of something
worrying the manager!

301
00:16:17,944 --> 00:16:19,444
Something is...

302
00:16:19,444 --> 00:16:20,774
...worrying the manager?

303
00:16:21,044 --> 00:16:22,744
Does anything come to mind?

304
00:16:22,744 --> 00:16:25,014
Uh, we might not be the right people to ask.

305
00:16:25,014 --> 00:16:26,484
Isn't there anything?

306
00:16:26,544 --> 00:16:28,984
Bakery Tirol's cakes are very popular.

307
00:16:29,154 --> 00:16:30,844
I'd say it's not work-related.

308
00:16:30,954 --> 00:16:32,284
Oh I see.

309
00:16:32,454 --> 00:16:34,314
Thank you very much!

310
00:16:34,454 --> 00:16:37,184
I-I think we'd better be going now.

311
00:16:38,964 --> 00:16:43,224
I'm out of here. I'm going to use
my own investigation network.

312
00:16:43,564 --> 00:16:45,124
Investigation network?

313
00:16:45,764 --> 00:16:47,464
What?!

314
00:16:47,464 --> 00:16:49,274
Why the heck would I involve myself in that?

315
00:16:49,274 --> 00:16:50,964
Be generous, Genko.

316
00:16:51,244 --> 00:16:53,934
If you're looking for a love
counselor, try someone else!

317
00:16:54,104 --> 00:16:57,304
Well then I guess I'll just pick
this up and head home.

318
00:16:57,644 --> 00:17:01,384
Why you! You only came here to eat
my Baumkuchen, didn't you?!

319
00:17:01,384 --> 00:17:02,584
You're absolutely right.

320
00:17:02,584 --> 00:17:03,514
What?!

321
00:17:03,514 --> 00:17:04,454
See ya!

322
00:17:05,384 --> 00:17:07,084
Good night.

323
00:17:13,794 --> 00:17:14,884
Yumi!

324
00:17:15,864 --> 00:17:17,064
Kobato?

325
00:17:17,064 --> 00:17:18,134
Good evening.

326
00:17:18,134 --> 00:17:19,404
What are you doing?

327
00:17:19,404 --> 00:17:20,364
I'm a detective!

328
00:17:20,364 --> 00:17:20,804
What?
I'm a detective!

329
00:17:20,804 --> 00:17:21,374
What?
What I have found out so far is
that Bakery Tirol's cakes

330
00:17:21,374 --> 00:17:23,904
What I have found out so far is
that Bakery Tirol's cakes

331
00:17:23,904 --> 00:17:26,674
are very popular and that the
manager is probably worried

332
00:17:26,674 --> 00:17:28,004
about something other than work.

333
00:17:29,114 --> 00:17:34,914
Oh! But Mr. Ueda always gives the little
children some chocolate for free.

334
00:17:34,914 --> 00:17:37,284
He's always considerate of
the health of other people.

335
00:17:37,284 --> 00:17:42,344
And everybody likes his cakes.
That's how much I found out.

336
00:17:42,924 --> 00:17:45,754
And I even got some chocolate myself!

337
00:17:45,864 --> 00:17:48,624
Mr. Ueda is kind to everyone.

338
00:17:57,574 --> 00:17:59,644
Yumi. We'll begin tailing him now!

339
00:17:59,644 --> 00:18:00,694
What?!

340
00:18:10,954 --> 00:18:13,754
Kobato, forget it. Let's go home.

341
00:18:13,754 --> 00:18:14,824
Huh?

342
00:18:14,824 --> 00:18:15,794
But...

343
00:18:16,724 --> 00:18:17,694
Huh?

344
00:18:23,394 --> 00:18:25,524
I wonder if he's meeting someone.

345
00:18:26,204 --> 00:18:30,174
We really shouldn't be following
him like this, but...

346
00:18:30,174 --> 00:18:32,404
Oh, someone has arrived.

347
00:18:36,114 --> 00:18:37,444
Who could that be?

348
00:18:38,484 --> 00:18:40,314
Is it someone you don't know?

349
00:18:40,484 --> 00:18:41,674
Never seen her.

350
00:18:43,054 --> 00:18:44,914
Maybe they're on a date!

351
00:18:45,024 --> 00:18:47,514
And maybe that's why he
couldn't tell me about her.

352
00:18:47,624 --> 00:18:49,294
What should I do, Kobato?

353
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:51,094
Please settle down, Yumi!

354
00:18:51,094 --> 00:18:53,094
Mr. Ueda will notice us.

355
00:18:53,094 --> 00:18:54,254
Yumi?

356
00:18:58,134 --> 00:18:59,324
Yumi!

357
00:19:04,744 --> 00:19:06,044
Yumi!

358
00:19:06,044 --> 00:19:07,094
Wait!

359
00:19:07,544 --> 00:19:08,664
Mr. Ueda.

360
00:19:09,914 --> 00:19:11,084
Kobato!

361
00:19:11,084 --> 00:19:12,284
Oww...

362
00:19:12,284 --> 00:19:13,374
Are you all right?

363
00:19:14,014 --> 00:19:15,544
I'm fine.

364
00:19:15,854 --> 00:19:18,714
But what I want to know is, who was
that person you were with?

365
00:19:21,624 --> 00:19:23,354
Actually that was an interview.

366
00:19:24,864 --> 00:19:26,554
For a job at the shop.

367
00:19:26,724 --> 00:19:29,064
A job? Why?

368
00:19:29,834 --> 00:19:33,704
Kobato's now helping out on the
weekends, but frankly,

369
00:19:33,704 --> 00:19:37,064
I haven't been able to give
you any time off, Yumi.

370
00:19:37,174 --> 00:19:38,264
Time off?

371
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:41,004
You must be very exhausted.

372
00:19:41,214 --> 00:19:44,144
And you working under such conditions
probably had something to do with your injury.

373
00:19:44,714 --> 00:19:48,304
Mr. Ueda... Then, that's what
you were worried about?

374
00:19:48,584 --> 00:19:49,674
Yes.

375
00:19:50,354 --> 00:19:57,694
You always work so hard for me, and I feel like
I've been taking advantage of that. I'm sorry.

376
00:19:58,064 --> 00:20:04,464
Oh, no. I really enjoy working with you.
I don't need any time off.

377
00:20:04,704 --> 00:20:09,034
I enjoy talking with the customers who
come to buy your cakes every day.

378
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:14,704
And I enjoy greeting you every day!
Besides, my injury...

379
00:20:15,974 --> 00:20:17,104
Well...

380
00:20:21,514 --> 00:20:23,744
That is very cute.

381
00:20:23,814 --> 00:20:25,844
Did you make this?

382
00:20:26,224 --> 00:20:32,124
Yes. I hurt myself all over
while practicing baking cakes.

383
00:20:32,694 --> 00:20:37,654
I wanted to help you out, so I decided to learn.

384
00:20:38,764 --> 00:20:40,494
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

385
00:20:42,974 --> 00:20:44,664
Do you mind if I try it?

386
00:20:46,544 --> 00:20:48,204
Ah, sure.

387
00:21:01,754 --> 00:21:02,984
It's good.

388
00:21:03,094 --> 00:21:04,354
Really?

389
00:21:05,124 --> 00:21:08,064
I've hired a new girl, which gives you more time.

390
00:21:08,264 --> 00:21:11,994
We can study baking cakes together.

391
00:21:13,534 --> 00:21:14,624
Yes!

392
00:21:22,344 --> 00:21:24,674
So, the case has been solved?

393
00:21:24,784 --> 00:21:27,874
Yes. Detective Kobato has solved the case.

394
00:21:28,354 --> 00:21:37,384
The manager wanted to give Yumi more time
off... but Yumi wanted to help him more.

395
00:21:37,894 --> 00:21:40,424
They were both being considerate for the other.

396
00:21:40,424 --> 00:21:43,364
It was a very beautiful case.

397
00:21:43,534 --> 00:21:44,764
Oh well. I can't complain.

398
00:21:45,404 --> 00:21:47,204
And I got my Baumkuchen.

399
00:21:47,204 --> 00:21:50,064
That Baumkuchen is not from Bakery Tirol, is it?

400
00:21:50,934 --> 00:21:54,434
And you brought it home once before.

401
00:21:55,044 --> 00:21:58,504
Does this have something to do with
your "investigation network"?

402
00:21:58,884 --> 00:22:01,374
Oh, that reminds me! Your score this time!

403
00:22:01,814 --> 00:22:04,084
I got to eat some cake, so I'll be extra
sweet and give you one hundred!

404
00:22:04,684 --> 00:22:06,244
Really?

405
00:22:09,154 --> 00:22:10,154
Fujimoto!

406
00:22:10,154 --> 00:22:11,024
What is it?

407
00:22:11,024 --> 00:22:12,024
I brought something for you!

408
00:22:12,024 --> 00:22:12,964
Huh?

409
00:22:12,964 --> 00:22:15,794
It's chocolate from the shop
that offered me a job.

410
00:22:16,294 --> 00:22:18,394
A job? You?

411
00:22:18,764 --> 00:22:25,004
I'll keep trying my best! So please take some
time off, or go to classes, or whatever.

412
00:22:26,244 --> 00:22:29,904
Well, I can't imagine anything good
happening with you trying your best.

413
00:22:31,714 --> 00:22:33,574
You are not nice...

414
00:22:34,814 --> 00:22:35,614
Hey.

415
00:22:38,424 --> 00:22:41,154
Don't try too hard to the extent
that you make yourself sick.

416
00:22:44,054 --> 00:22:46,324
Could you possibly be worrying about me?

417
00:22:46,324 --> 00:22:47,194
Not at all.

418
00:22:47,194 --> 00:22:48,864
Thank you very much.

419
00:22:48,864 --> 00:22:51,164
Right now, do something about
that scribble on your face.

420
00:22:51,164 --> 00:22:52,764
Th-This is my hundred points!

421
00:22:52,764 --> 00:22:54,634
What are you talking about? It's scribble.

422
00:22:54,634 --> 00:22:58,344
No it isn't! You only get fifty
points because you're mean!

423
00:22:58,344 --> 00:22:59,734
What on earth are you talking about?

424
00:23:01,344 --> 00:23:08,974
Everyone dreams of flying

425
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:16,254
But they let gravity trick them

426
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:24,364
Honestly, everyone is already able to fly

427
00:23:26,604 --> 00:23:32,934
I bet the reason that child looks so terribly sad

428
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:36,844
Is because he

429
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:43,974
Accidentally lost his shadow somewhere

430
00:23:44,154 --> 00:23:46,674
In that case

431
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:50,954
If I could just tell you, "Thank you,"

432
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,834
And you laugh and reply, "Thank you"

433
00:23:54,834 --> 00:24:02,164
That exchange would fill you with joy

434
00:24:02,704 --> 00:24:06,934
It would make you feel so happy

435
00:24:07,244 --> 00:24:11,484
There's nothing to worry about

436
00:24:11,484 --> 00:24:15,574
Since we're together

437
00:24:17,354 --> 00:24:23,294
It's strange how I'm crying

438
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:26,064
Even though I'm happy

439
00:24:26,064 --> 00:24:29,034
Next episode
...Silver Eyes.
Even though I'm happy

440
00:24:29,034 --> 00:24:30,754
Next episode
...Silver Eyes.

